# Converted to the revised ten-section template (plus section 11); content and tables carried from the previous version.
BOOK = 'Zechariah'
TESTAMENT = 'Old Testament'
GENRE = 'prophets'
SUBTITLE = 'Return to the LORD, the Coming King, and the LORD King Over All the Earth'
SECTIONS = [(1, 'Book Setting & Program Identity', [('p', 'This section introduces you to the book by explaining who wrote it, who received it, and what was happening when it was written. It also shows you which of God’s programs the book belongs to — Israel’s prophetic program or the Body of Christ’s mystery program. Knowing the setting and the program identity helps you read the book in its proper context and understand how its teachings fit into the larger story of Scripture.'), ('p', 'Zechariah is “the word of the LORD unto Zechariah, the son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo the prophet” in the second year of Darius (Zech. 1:1). The book moves through night visions, the high priest and the BRANCH, the King who comes lowly on an ass, the house of David and the Spirit of grace, the fountain opened for sin, and the day when the LORD fights the nations, stands on the mount of Olives and is king over all the earth (Zech. 3:8; 9:9; 12:10; 13:1; 14:3–4, 9).'), ('box', 'Program Identity:', 'This book belongs entirely to the Prophecy Program, where the LORD speaks to Judah, Jerusalem, the house of David and the remnant about return, the King and the Kingdom (Zech. 2:10; 8:3; 12:10; 14:16).')]),
(2, 'Narrative Flow of Zechariah', [('p', 'This section gives you a simple walkthrough of how the book unfolds. Instead of diving into details right away, it shows the major movements in the book — how its message begins, how it develops, and how it builds toward its close. Seeing the flow of the book helps you understand the big picture before you study the individual passages.'), ('h3', 'Movement 1 — Return to the LORD (Chs. 1–2)'), ('p', 'The people are told to turn to the LORD, and the LORD says He will dwell in the midst of the daughter of Zion (Zech. 1:1, 3; 2:10).'), ('h3', 'Movement 2 — Joshua and the BRANCH (Chs. 3–6)'), ('p', 'Joshua the high priest stands before the LORD, and the BRANCH is promised, who shall build the temple and sit and rule upon his throne (Zech. 3:8; 4:6; 6:12–13).'), ('h3', 'Movement 3 — Truth, Mercy, and Zion Restored (Chs. 7–8)'), ('p', 'The LORD says He is returned unto Zion, and the nations take hold of him that is a Jew (Zech. 7:9; 8:3, 16, 23).'), ('h3', 'Movement 4 — The King Cometh (Chs. 9–11)'), ('p', 'The daughter of Zion is told that her King cometh, lowly and riding upon an ass (Zech. 9:9–10).'), ('h3', 'Movement 5 — The Spirit, the Fountain, and the Day (Chs. 12–14)'), ('p', 'The LORD pours the spirit of grace on the house of David, opens a fountain for sin, and becomes king over all the earth (Zech. 12:10; 13:1; 14:3–4, 9, 16, 20).')]),
(3, 'Program Themes in Zechariah', [('p', 'This section highlights the major ideas emphasized in the book — the big doctrinal themes that shape how Israel should think and live under the covenants. These themes are not verse-by-verse explanations; they are the book’s main emphases, the repeated ideas God wants Israel to carry forward. Seeing these themes together helps you understand the book’s message before you look at the individual truths in the tables.'), ('ol', ['<b>Turn Ye Unto Me</b> — “Turn ye unto me, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will turn unto you” (Zech. 1:3).', '<b>Not by Might</b> — “Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts” (Zech. 4:6).', '<b>The BRANCH</b> — “Behold the man whose name is The BRANCH; and he shall grow up out of his place, and he shall build the temple of the LORD” (Zech. 6:12).', '<b>The LORD Dwells in Zion</b> — “I am returned unto Zion, and will dwell in the midst of Jerusalem” (Zech. 8:3).', '<b>The King Cometh</b> — “Behold, thy King cometh unto thee: he is just, and having salvation” (Zech. 9:9).', '<b>The Spirit of Grace</b> — “I will pour upon the house of David, and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the spirit of grace and of supplications” (Zech. 12:10).', '<b>King Over All the Earth</b> — “The LORD shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one LORD, and his name one” (Zech. 14:9).'])]),
(4, 'Christ in Zechariah', [('p', 'This section gathers what the book teaches about Christ — through foreshadowing, typology, and prophetic anticipation. These statements help you see the book’s Christ-centered trajectory before you study the doctrinal truths in detail. By collecting these points together, you get a clear picture of how Zechariah points to Christ.'), ('ol', ['<b>The BRANCH</b> — The BRANCH who builds the temple and sits and rules upon his throne (Zech. 3:8; 6:12–13) is reported as written.', '<b>The King on an Ass</b> — Zechariah 9:9 is quoted in Matthew 21:5; the New Testament quotation is read in its own chapter.', '<b>They Shall Look on Me</b> — “They shall look upon me whom they have pierced” (Zech. 12:10) is reported as written, with the pouring of the spirit of grace on the house of David and Jerusalem.'])]),
(5, 'Israel, the Law, and the Covenants in Zechariah', [('p', 'This section helps you see how Zechariah speaks about Israel, the law, and the covenants without mixing programs. Zechariah operates within Israel’s prophetic framework. By gathering these points together, this section shows you how to read Zechariah in its own setting — as an Israel-program book — while recognizing what it says (and does not say) about the Body of Christ.'), ('p', 'Zechariah reinforces Israel’s:'), ('ul', ['Joshua the high priest and the BRANCH (Zech. 3:8; 6:12–13)', 'the daughter of Zion, Jerusalem and the holy mountain (Zech. 2:10; 8:3)', 'the house of David and the inhabitants of Jerusalem (Zech. 12:10; 13:1)', 'the nations coming up to worship the King, the LORD of hosts (Zech. 14:16)']), ('p', 'All content belongs exclusively to the Prophecy Program.')]),
(6, 'Israel-Program Distinctions', [('p', 'This section highlights the teachings in Zechariah that belong uniquely to Israel’s prophetic program — truths rooted in prophecy, covenant promises, national identity, and God’s dealings with Israel. By gathering these together, this section helps you see how Zechariah contributes to Israel’s story without borrowing from the Body-of-Christ program.'), ('ul', ['The Word of the LORD — “came the word of the LORD unto Zechariah.” (Zech. 1:1).', 'The BRANCH — “I will bring forth my servant the BRANCH.” (Zech. 3:8).', 'The Temple Built — “he shall build the temple of the LORD.” (Zech. 6:12).', 'Seated and Ruling — “shall sit and rule upon his throne.” (Zech. 6:13).', 'Dwelling in Jerusalem — “I am returned unto Zion, and will dwell in the midst of Jerusalem.” (Zech. 8:3).', 'The Nations and the Jew — “ten men shall take hold out of all languages of the nations, even shall take hold of the skirt of him that is a Jew.” (Zech. 8:23).', 'The King Cometh — “thy King cometh unto thee.” (Zech. 9:9).', 'Dominion Sea to Sea — “his dominion shall be from sea even to sea.” (Zech. 9:10).', 'Spirit of Grace — “I will pour upon the house of David, and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the spirit of grace and of supplications.” (Zech. 12:10).', 'A Fountain Opened — “there shall be a fountain opened to the house of David and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem for sin and for uncleanness.” (Zech. 13:1).', 'Feet on the Mount — “his feet shall stand in that day upon the mount of Olives.” (Zech. 14:4).', 'King Over All — “the LORD shall be king over all the earth.” (Zech. 14:9).', 'The Feast of Tabernacles — “go up from year to year to worship the King, the LORD of hosts, and to keep the feast of tabernacles.” (Zech. 14:16).'])]),
(7, 'Truths Table: What Zechariah Says', [('p', 'This table gathers the key statements, instructions, and teachings in Zechariah and shows which ones belong to Israel’s prophetic program. Each row lists a truth from the book, explains what it says, and identifies its program identity based on Israel’s covenant setting. This helps you see, at a glance, what Zechariah teaches directly to Israel and keeps those truths separate from universal principles that apply more broadly.'), ('table', ['Category', 'Truth Revealed in Zechariah', 'Program Identity', 'Scripture'], [['The Word of the LORD', '“came the word of the LORD unto Zechariah.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 1:1'], ['The BRANCH', '“I will bring forth my servant the BRANCH.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 3:8'], ['The Temple Built', '“he shall build the temple of the LORD.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 6:12'], ['Seated and Ruling', '“shall sit and rule upon his throne.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 6:13'], ['Dwelling in Jerusalem', '“I am returned unto Zion, and will dwell in the midst of Jerusalem.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 8:3'], ['The Nations and the Jew', '“ten men shall take hold out of all languages of the nations, even shall take hold of the skirt of him that is a Jew.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 8:23'], ['The King Cometh', '“thy King cometh unto thee.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 9:9'], ['Dominion Sea to Sea', '“his dominion shall be from sea even to sea.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 9:10'], ['Spirit of Grace', '“I will pour upon the house of David, and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the spirit of grace and of supplications.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 12:10'], ['A Fountain Opened', '“there shall be a fountain opened to the house of David and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem for sin and for uncleanness.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 13:1'], ['Feet on the Mount', '“his feet shall stand in that day upon the mount of Olives.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 14:4'], ['King Over All', '“the LORD shall be king over all the earth.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 14:9'], ['The Feast of Tabernacles', '“go up from year to year to worship the King, the LORD of hosts, and to keep the feast of tabernacles.”', 'Israel / Kingdom / Prophecy Explicit Truth', 'Zech. 14:16']], [20, 34, 26, 20])]),
(8, 'Universal Truths Table (All People, All Time)', [('p', 'This table gathers the truths in Zechariah that apply to everyone, not just Israel. These are principles rooted in God’s character — things that hold true across all programs and all ages. By separating these universal truths from Israel’s covenant-specific instructions, this section helps you see what Zechariah teaches all believers everywhere and what it teaches Israel in its own setting.'), ('table', ['Universal Truth', 'Description', 'Scripture'], [['Turn to Him', '“Turn ye unto me, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will turn unto you.”', 'Zech. 1:3'], ['By His Spirit', '“Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.”', 'Zech. 4:6'], ['True Judgment and Mercy', '“Execute true judgment, and shew mercy and compassions every man to his brother.”', 'Zech. 7:9'], ['Speak the Truth', '“Speak ye every man the truth to his neighbour.”', 'Zech. 8:16'], ['No Evil in the Heart', '“let none of you imagine evil in your hearts against his neighbour.”', 'Zech. 8:17']], [28, 48, 24])]),
(9, 'Program-Safe Application Grid', [('p', 'This section shows how to apply the teachings of Zechariah without mixing programs. The applications come from Israel’s covenant story and from universal truths that apply to everyone. By keeping the applications tied to what the book actually says — and not borrowing commands from Israel’s covenants for the Body of Christ — this grid helps you respond to Zechariah in a way that is faithful to its setting, clear, and safe.'), ('ol', ['<b>Turn to the LORD</b> — He promises to turn to those who turn (Zech. 1:3).', '<b>Rely on His Spirit</b> — Not by might nor power (Zech. 4:6).', '<b>Execute true judgment and show mercy</b> — Every man to his brother (Zech. 7:9).', '<b>Speak the truth</b> — To your neighbour (Zech. 8:16).', '<b>Keep evil out of the heart</b> — Toward your neighbour (Zech. 8:17).'])]),
(10, 'Teaching Outline for Zechariah', [('p', 'This outline gives you a teacher-ready structure for presenting the book. It follows the narrative movements and highlights the major themes, making it easy to teach Zechariah in classes, small groups, or personal study.'), ('olr', ['Return to the LORD (Chs. 1–2) — Turn ye unto me. <i>(Zech. 1:3; 2:10)</i>', 'Joshua and the BRANCH (Chs. 3–6) — Not by might. <i>(Zech. 3:8; 4:6; 6:12–13)</i>', 'Truth, Mercy, and Zion Restored (Chs. 7–8) — The LORD in Jerusalem. <i>(Zech. 7:9; 8:3, 16–17, 23)</i>', 'The King Cometh (Chs. 9–11) — Lowly on an ass. <i>(Zech. 9:9–10)</i>', 'The Spirit, the Fountain, and the Day (Chs. 12–14) — King over all the earth. <i>(Zech. 12:10; 13:1; 14:4, 9, 16)</i>'])]),
(11, 'Companion Usage and Study Suggestions', [('h3', 'How to Use This Companion in Personal Study'), ('p', 'This Companion is designed to walk alongside you as you read Zechariah, helping you see both the prophetic structure of the book and the timeless truths rooted in God’s character. Use it slowly, chapter by chapter, letting the narrative movements, themes, and universal truths deepen your understanding. The Program-Safe Applications will guide your heart toward truth, mercy, and dependence on the LORD’s Spirit without confusing Israel’s covenant commands with the Body of Christ’s calling today.'), ('h3', 'How to Use This Companion in Small Groups or Classes'), ('p', 'This Companion provides a clear, structured framework that makes teaching Zechariah simple and accessible. Each section gives you ready-to-use material: narrative movements for overview, prophecy-program themes for doctrinal clarity, universal truths for discussion, and a pastoral teaching outline for weekly lessons. Use the tables to help your group distinguish Israel’s covenant identity from universal principles, and use the Program-Safe Application Grid to foster meaningful, Christ-centered conversation.'), ('h3', 'How This Companion Fits Within the Acts Overlap Theology Series'), ('p', 'This Companion is part of a larger series designed to help believers read every book of Scripture without blurring God’s prophetic program for Israel and His mystery program for the Body of Christ. Within the Acts Overlap Theology Series, Zechariah stands firmly in Israel’s covenant story, yet it still reveals universal truths that shape Christian character today. This Companion shows you how to honor the book’s prophetic context while drawing out the timeless principles that apply to all believers in every age.')])]
